What changed
- lib/MCP/Hub/Upstream.pm: new private helper _error_message(). It reads the
  "message" of a JSON-RPC error only when the error is a hash, otherwise it
  stringifies or JSON-encodes it. The helper is eval-guarded and can never
  throw, so the promise is always settled -- a deleted pending entry is never
  left unsettled.
- lib/MCP/Hub/Upstream/Stdio.pm: _on_response rejects with that message.
- lib/MCP/Hub/Upstream/Http.pm: _on_message rejects with that message.
- lib/MCP/Hub/Upstream/Http.pm: the two die() calls in _http_request_p use it
  as well. Not named in the card, but the same defect class on the Streamable
  HTTP path (a non-object error there died in the response handler, so the
  caller saw the raw Perl error instead of the upstream message), so it is
  fixed too. No public API or visible behaviour changed otherwise.

